      "summary": "A candidate 2K epoxy-polyamide BOM (DGEBA-828 resin / Ancamide 2353 polyamide curing agent / zinc-phosphate+talc pigment / xylene+n-butanol solvent blend) is built from real cited amphora-ingredient-library facts. The hardener mass is set to the exact EEW/AHEW stoichiometric equivalence (1.000x, no excess amine). Pigment loading (PVC) and a solvent A/B split fraction are solved algebraically so the mixed system lands the charter's 1:1-by-volume mix ratio and target volume-solids %. The resulting BOM is then INDEPENDENTLY re-derived by a forward_recompute() function that only ever sees the final (name, mass_g, density_g_ml, nonvolatile) row table -- it has no knowledge of the PVC/stoichiometry/solvent-split design algebra used to build that table -- exactly as a bench chemist reading the BOM off a page would recompute volume-solids%, VOC g/L, and mix ratio. A second, exact-rational (fractions.Fraction) recompute of the same forward summation cross-checks the float result to rule out rounding masking a bound violation."
